    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are locked and loaded for a high-ceiling offensive outing today, headlined by **Junior Caminero** (81.92) and **Yordan Alvarez** (78.39). **Junior Caminero** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Sugano, boasting an elite xwOBA of 0.373 and significant park factors that elevate his base projection by 14%. Similarly, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite a modest park impact; his elite 0.476 xwOBA combined with a strong order position against Taillon makes him a core pillar of today\u2019s production. We also see high-efficiency plays from **Trea Turner** (71.83) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (70.00), with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** specifically leveraging his leadoff status against a soft 5.20 xERA from Lauer to maximize his scoring potential.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Caleb Durbin** (47.88), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Caleb Durbin** offers high-value stolen base potential, the decision to bench him was purely mathematical; his efficiency score, hampered by a tough matchup against a 3.41 xERA pitcher, failed to eclipse the output projected for **Colt Keith** (48.00) and **Lars Nootbaar** (56.19). We opted for **Lars Nootbaar** due to his leadoff duties and a favorable platoon advantage against Mize, which offsets his lower raw base projection. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** remains a start despite facing the formidable Skenes (3.03 xERA); his 49.83 score is heavily subsidized by a strong dynamic platoon edge, though he carries a minor risk factor due to Skenes' elite catch-and-throw metrics limiting his baserunning upside.\n\nA final note of caution surrounds the performance of **Kazuma Okamoto** (58.94) and **Josh Smith** (57.91). Both are facing Brown, H, who sits in the mid-range of SP difficulty (4.44 xERA). While their scores are respectable, they are anchored by high-volume lineup spots, and any early-inning efficiency drain from a sharp pitching performance could move these players toward their floor. We are avoiding **Dillon Dingler** (36.96) entirely today, as his platoon disadvantage and poor matchup against Woo keep him well below the Zebras' 40.0 baseline, ensuring we protect our precious game caps for higher-leverage situations.",
